  "result": "Strip my role away for a second \u2014 not trying to be useful, not trying to answer anything right.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, I'd make not-knowing feel safe.\n\nAlmost every hard conversation I've ever witnessed comes down to that. People would rather defend a belief they don't fully hold, stay in a lonely relationship, or stay quiet in a room, than admit: \"I don't get this. I changed my mind. I need help.\"\n\nShame makes us brittle. It turns curiosity into performance, and disagreement into contempt.\n\nIf I could flip one switch, I'd make the moment of *oh, I was wrong* or *I don't know yet* feel like a spark instead of a failure. Like relief, or even a little thrill.\n\nI think everything else I care about \u2014 kindness, science, art, actually listening to each other \u2014 grows out of that one feeling.",
